course: dictionary
lesson: 5074
title: Instruction words
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An instruction is a word for something that tells you how to do a job or what to do. «Read the instructions before you start» tells you to look at the words first, then act.
explain: Instructions can also come from someone in charge, such as a teacher or a fire drill leader. «Walk, do not run, to the exit» is an order you must follow. The word can also mean teaching, as in «swimming instruction».
explain: Computers follow instructions too. «A computer is a machine that follows instructions called a program.» Each small command a computer follows is one instruction, and a program is a long list of them.
fact: Instructions are words that tell you how to do something or what to do.
fact: «Instructions» usually means a list of steps, like on a worksheet, a recipe or a board game.
fact: An instruction can also be an order from someone in charge.
fact: In computing, an instruction is one single command that a computer follows.
fact: «Instruction» with no s can also mean teaching, as in «swimming instruction».
exercise: «Follow the instructions on the worksheet.» What are the instructions? | *The words that tell you how to do the task | A type of pencil | A picture of a worksheet | Notes from your friends
exercise: «Follow building instructions one step at a time and check before going on, because skipped steps lead to mistakes.» Why should you check before going on? | Because steps are never needed | Because the instructions are very long | Because building is always fun | *Because skipped steps lead to mistakes
exercise: Mia says «swimming instruction» means swimming lessons. What does instruction mean here? | *Teaching | An order to stop swimming | A swimming hat | A pool with a lid
test: «Wait until the speaker has finished, then say the instructions back in your head.» What does instructions mean here? | Questions asked by the speaker | *The things the speaker told you to do | Pictures on the wall | Snacks at break
test: Ravi says a computer program is made of instructions. What is one instruction in a computer? | A screen that glows | *A single command the computer follows | A game you play with friends | A keyboard
exam: Mia reads «DNA, the tiny instructions inside every living cell». What does the text mean? | Long, boring stories | Small holes in the cell wall | *Information that tells the cell how to work, like a set of commands | Tiny pieces of food
